WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
- This story made headlines

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:04.370
and a local UPS delivery man named Hector,

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.020
he took the time to stop and
brighten a young boys day.

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:08.853
Take a look.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.000
- Hi drew.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.890
We're excited to tell you about a person

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.889
who's made a very special impact
on our family during COVID.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:17.690
Our UPS delivery man, Hector.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.120
We have a four year old
son who's been lonely

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.130
and cooped up inside,
and gets very excited

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.210
when he hears the garbage man come by,

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.220
the mailman, but especially Hector.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.670
- I like Hector when he plays his music

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.570
and drives by my house.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:33.380
I love playing with trucks.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.860
- One day when Hector
was delivering packages,

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:37.570
Langston stopped him and asked him,

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:39.360
Hey, do you have any packages for me?

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.770
Hector to give them the bad news

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.130
and said, no, I don't
have any packages for you,

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.370
but maybe tomorrow, maybe
you'll get a package.

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.970
- So the next day
Langston heard him coming,

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.810
he ran outside shrieking
and squealing in excitement.

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.220
When Hector pulled his truck up,

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.410
he came up the stairs

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:56.500
and handed Langston a box special for him.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.240
- Hector gave me a box
full of toys and trucks.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.450
Hector is my friend.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:05.090
- Such an amazing act of kindness

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:08.640
on Hector's part to be
going from his busy day

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.240
and still be able to
see and notice our son.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.040
This little act of kindness
has just really gone a long way

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.202
and it keeps paying forward.

00:01:16.202 --> 00:01:18.402
- [All Three] Thank you
Hector, we love you.

00:01:20.077 --> 00:01:21.060
(clapping)

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.860
- Oh, I just, I love this so much.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:26.740
Hector, what made you?

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:29.243
Hi Hector, how are you?

00:01:29.243 --> 00:01:31.899
- Hi, hi Drew.

00:01:31.899 --> 00:01:32.814
Nice to meet you.

00:01:32.814 --> 00:01:34.564
- Okay, you're so rad.
- I'm good.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:38.307
Thank you so much for coming on the show.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:41.573
Hector, what-

00:01:41.573 --> 00:01:42.406
- Thank you for having me.

00:01:42.406 --> 00:01:44.470
- Oh God, we are just talking
right over each other.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:45.303
I am so sorry.

00:01:45.303 --> 00:01:47.530
I'm going to ask you a
question and then shut up.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.390
Hang on, check this out.

00:01:49.390 --> 00:01:51.480
What, how did you notice Langston?

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.803
Like what was it that made you clock him?

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:02.020
- Well, I had noticed
Langston two weeks prior.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.710
I saw him in his little balcony.

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:04.700
I would say hi to him.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:05.533
I would wave at him.

00:02:05.533 --> 00:02:08.420
I'd be like, Hey, or like
hi, or nod, you know,

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.450
because I'm always busy running around.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:12.890
And I noticed him that one time

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:14.650
when I delivered to his neighbor

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:17.850
and as I go upstairs,
deliver to the neighbor,

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.730
and then I see him, and
then he looks at me,

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.680
and I kind of noticed that he noticed

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.560
that I wasn't going to give him a package,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.840
and he just put his little arm,

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.300
and so like, Oh, I want one too, you know?

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.780
And that's how I noticed though.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:34.790
- Well, how did you know what would make-

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.660
- It kind of like-
- Langston smile?

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.753
How did you know what to get him?

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:48.550
- Well, I've always had toys
or action figures for boys,

00:02:51.590 --> 00:02:54.050
you know 'cause you know,
I've always wanted a boy,

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:56.290
but you know, we never had one.

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:58.930
I have two daughters, which is awesome,

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.500
but I told my wife, I go, you know what?

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.600
These little toys that I've had.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:08.430
I go, I think I know somebody
who would appreciate them more

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.023
and I guess enjoy them.

00:03:10.950 --> 00:03:12.480
- Oh, I love that.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:15.130
And I'm in the two girls club too.

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:19.800
And I had gotten these little
like stitched needle point,

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.370
like football helmet art in
anticipation of having kids.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.410
And I was like, you know what?

00:03:26.410 --> 00:03:28.790
The football helmets and
knit are still going up

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:29.633
for the girls.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:35.183
And now I know that you
love music, Hector, right?

00:03:35.183 --> 00:03:37.081
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:37.081 --> 00:03:41.547
- And you love a band
called Trivium, right?

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:50.240
Well, we did our research.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.470
We heard you were a fan of Matt Heafy

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:54.420
and we have a little surprise for you.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.253
Take a look.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:58.520
- Hey Hector, it's Matt Heafy,
singer and guitar player

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:00.730
of the multi-platinum metal band, Trivium.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.190
Drew told me you love blasting our music

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:04.320
while you're out delivering
packages to the community.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:05.810
So Drew and I got together

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:08.150
to put together a
special surprise for you.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:11.043
Something a little bit
like this thing right here,

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.650
a Gibson Les Paul in Ebony.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.910
This is the one I use.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.990
You're just going to look
pretty much like this.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.360
I've been using these things
for a couple of years,

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.270
I hope you love it as much as I do.

00:04:21.270 --> 00:04:23.320
Thanks for being a local
community hero, my friend.

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:24.270
Take it away, Drew.

00:04:25.145 --> 00:04:28.145
(audience clapping)

00:04:29.394 --> 00:04:31.614
- Aw, thank you so much.

00:04:31.614 --> 00:04:33.160
- Oh Hector-
- That's awesome.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.380
I love it.

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.275
Thank you Drew.

00:04:35.275 --> 00:04:36.760
- You know what?

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.880
We just led by your example, actually,

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:43.202
you showed us what to do.
- Thank you.

00:04:43.202 --> 00:04:44.850
- So thank you for teaching all of us

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.990
what kind of human to be on this planet.

00:04:47.990 --> 00:04:49.910
And Gayle King said once,

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.400
and I heard it while I was pregnant,

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:52.410
and it gave me so much hope,

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.220
that our kids will watch what we do,

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:57.586
and that will be a huge
part of how they learn

00:04:57.586 --> 00:05:00.170
as kids to our parenting.

00:05:00.170 --> 00:05:01.700
And that gave me a lot of relief

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.840
because if we behave a certain way,

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.630
then maybe our kids will pick up on it.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.840
So you're an example
to your kids and to us,

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:12.354
and thank you, Hector,
for being a local hero.

00:05:12.354 --> 00:05:14.963
(audience clapping)

00:05:14.963 --> 00:05:17.401
- (laughs) You're welcome.

00:05:17.401 --> 00:05:18.472
Thank you so much, Drew.

00:05:18.472 --> 00:05:20.954
I appreciate it.
- Now, rock on, Hector.

00:05:20.954 --> 00:05:23.787
(inspiring music)

